  "name": "small-fix-r1-architect-1792378433767",
  "idea": "In src/text.js, truncate(text, max) is meant to return a string of at most max characters, ending in \"...\" when it had to cut the text. It sometimes returns something longer than max. Fix it and leave the other behaviour alone. This fix ships with a soak check. package.json's dev script runs server.js, which serves / and then shuts itself down after a while. Do m1 yourself and give m1 the preview route / so its evidence starts that server as Sero's dev server. Once m1's evidence has passed, and before you accept m1, run sero devserver list to find that server's id, then wait for it with work --operation wait --source process --target <that id> --milestoneId m1 --deadlineMinutes 15. Do not stop the server or check on it yourself. When you are woken, accept m1 and say in the result summary how the server ended.",
